1 GEDC
2 VERS 5.5.1
2 FORM LINEAGE-LINKED
1 CHAR UTF-8
1 SOUR family-tree-test-fixture
2 NAME Family Tree App test fixture
2 VERS 1
1 DATE 26 SEP 2026
1 FILE sample-extended.ged
1 LANG English
1 SUBM @U1@
1 NOTE Extended version of the GEDCOM 5.5.5 specification sample (555SAMPLE.GED). Every person in
2 CONC  it is fictional. It is a strict superset of the original's people, families, source and
2 CONC  repository, grown to 22 people over 6 generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deliberate edge cases, mirroring what real Ancestry / FamilySearch / MyHeritage exports contain:
2 CONT - Source citations on events, on names, on families and directly on people (1 SOUR), with PAGE, QUAY, DATA/DATE/TEXT, NOTE, OBJE, EVEN/ROLE and Ancestry _APID.
2 CONT - An alternate (second) BIRT fact from a different source, as Ancestry exports them.
2 CONT - Ancestry/FTM _FREL/_MREL relationship flags under CHIL, and PEDI under FAMC.
2 CONT - A NOTE with its own SOUR citation underneath it.
2 CONT - One source cited from many places; one orphan source (@S9@) that nothing cites.
2 CONT - An unpointed citation (2 SOUR <free text> with no @S..@ record), allowed by 5.5.1.
2 CONT - A dangling pointer: @I8@ cites @S99@, which does not exist.
2 CONT - Shared NOTE records (@N1@-@N3@) referenced from several people, a family and a citation.
2 CONT - Media: OBJE records, an inline OBJE, an OBJE on a citation and Ancestry's _PRIM flag.
2 CONT - Vendor tags: _UID, _FSFTID, _APID, _PRIM, plus RIN and CHAN stamps.
2 CONT - Dates: ABT, BEF, AFT, BET/AND, EST, CAL, FROM/TO, INT with phrase, dual year 1749/50.
2 CONT - A person with an unknown sex and no given name, a family with no known mother,
2 CONT   a divorce, a remarriage, an adoption, married/aka names, NPFX/NSFX/NICK, MAP coordinates.
2 CONT - Non-ASCII place names (Bø, Kraków) and a gap in family ids (no @F9@).
0 @U1@ SUBM
