0 @N1@ NOTE Williams line: research notes.
1 CONT The Williams family came from Llanfair, Montgomeryshire. Rev. Evan Williams was curate there;
1 CONT his son Thomas emigrated via Liverpool in 1819 and settled in Weston, Connecticut.
1 CONT Welsh patronymic naming means earlier generations may not use Williams as a fixed surname.
0 @N2@ NOTE Census and death-record ages for Robert are consistent with a 1822 birth; Mary Ann's
1 CONC  age in 1850 (22) puts her birth before 1828, hence the BEF 1828 date.
0 @N3@ NOTE Robert and Mary Ann's marriage place (Rapid City, SD) is copied from the original
1 CONC  GEDCOM sample and is almost certainly wrong for a Connecticut couple in 1859.
1 CONT Kept as-is so the fixture remains a superset of 555SAMPLE.GED.
